course: dictionary
lesson: 10733
title: The word upper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Upper means higher up, or above something else of the same kind. It is an adjective, so it describes a noun: the upper floor is the floor that is higher up in a building. Its opposite is lower, so when you see upper, think of the top part.
explain: Upper can also mean nearer the top of a place, a river or a land. «The upper Nile» means the part of the river nearer its source, far from where it reaches the sea. Look at the words around upper to find which part of the thing is meant.
explain: Upper can mean higher in rank or level, as in «the upper school», which means the older classes. In the phrase «the upper hand», upper means having the advantage. Context tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Upper means higher up, or above something else of the same kind.
fact: «Upper case» letters are capital letters, such as A, B and C.
fact: «Lower case» letters are the small ones, so upper and lower are opposites.
fact: The upper layer of soil is called topsoil.
fact: Other phrases with upper: «upper lip», «upper floor», and «the upper hand», which means the advantage.
exercise: «What makes a rodent is its teeth: two upper and two lower front teeth that never stop growing.» In this sentence, which teeth are the upper ones? | The back teeth at the bottom of the mouth | The teeth that never grow | The long pointed teeth at the sides | *The front teeth at the top, above the lower ones
exercise: «The sloth bear of India and Sri Lanka has a gap where two upper front teeth are missing.» What does upper mean here? | Newest and most modern | Far away across the sea | Very loud and noisy | *Higher up, in the top jaw
exercise: «Upper case» letters are the ones you use for names and the start of sentences. What is another name for upper case letters? | Small letters | *Capital letters | Letters with curly tails | Letters written in pencil
test: Which phrase in this lesson means having the advantage? | *the upper hand | upper floor | upper lip | upper case
test: «The lub-dub sound is the heart's valves snapping shut: «lub» when the valves between the upper and lower chambers close.» What does upper mean here? | Very loud | Newest and most modern | Left side only | *Higher up, nearer the top
exam: «The narwhal's tusk is a tooth, usually the left upper canine.» In this sentence, upper means | Very long and pointed | *Higher up in the mouth, in the top jaw | Shiny and smooth | Older and more experienced
